  TypeDecl
    LineComment "// Type values. Every type symbol is, in value position, a compile-time value —"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// immutable, side-effect-free, of the builtin type `type` (the metatype, with"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// type : type). A bare type name reifies to one (const t = sbyte), and the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// `type` keyword names the metatype as a value. Type values exist only at"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// compile time: they fold and are gone before any runtime. This is the basis the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// masterdata layer is rebuilt on (a master is a type value with a master"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// descriptor); 0001 lands the representation, member resolution unifies onto it,"
